  "official_std_basis": "Rust 1.96 documents platform-dependent SystemTime precision: Windows uses 100ns intervals and Linux can represent 1ns. The Windows checked duration conversion divides subsecond nanoseconds by 100 before subtracting interval counts.",
  "changes": [
    "Keep the exact original -1 second, -1 millisecond and 999999999 nanosecond assertions against an explicitly constructed Timestamp one nanosecond before the epoch.",
    "Independently exercise SystemTime one 100ns tick before the epoch, assert the full Timestamp object, and round-trip through the new fallible to_system_time method.",
    "Always execute the 1ns SystemTime subtraction request. Compare its decoded signed interval to the actual standard-library duration and require an exact SystemTime round-trip; exact 1ns native coverage remains on platforms that represent it."
  ],
